Android 15 manual-code accessibility selector regression

- The hosted rerun found that `TYPE_NUMBER_VARIATION_PASSWORD` alone did not expose the code EditText as a masked accessibility node. `MainActivity` now also applies `PasswordTransformationMethod` explicitly, preserving the six-digit numeric keyboard and masking entered codes.
- Rebuilt the phone preview and instrumentation APKs from this source with `sh android/build.sh` and `sh android/test/build.sh` -> both passed. `apksigner verify` passed for each; `aapt2 dump badging` confirmed package `com.fainir.accountaccess.phone`, version `1`, target SDK `36`.
- The hosted Android 11/15 run for the previous source still failed its masked-field assertion; the above source change requires a fresh emulator run before this flow is considered verified.
- `ACCOUNT_ACCESS_JAVA_HOME=/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@17/libexec/openjdk.jdk/Contents/Home sh android/build.sh` -> passed; produced the development preview APK in a new ignored `dist/android/` directory.
- `ACCOUNT_ACCESS_JAVA_HOME=/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@17/libexec/openjdk.jdk/Contents/Home sh android/test/build.sh` -> passed.
- `apksigner verify` -> passed for both the phone preview APK and instrumentation APK.
- This Mac has no Android API 35 emulator image; no physical Android device was connected. Hosted emulator rerun is required to qualify the updated accessibility selector.
- The test now locates the masked login-code EditText by its fixed visible hint when Android omits the password field's content description; it asserts the view remains an EditText and password-masked before entering the synthetic test code.
- Hosted run 40929994170 reproduced `masked=false, input_type=18` on both API 30 and API 35 even after explicitly setting `PasswordTransformationMethod`. The field retained its numeric password input type, but neither emulator exposed the password semantic bit.
- `MainActivity` now keeps the real password transformation and explicitly marks the accessibility node as a password through the view delegate. This preserves the `EditText` class, numeric keyboard and six-digit limit while ensuring assistive technology receives password semantics.
- Rebuilt `dist/android/Account-Access-Phone-preview.apk` and `dist/android/Account-Access-Phone-tests.apk`; both build scripts and `apksigner verify` passed. Hosted API 30/35 validation of the accessibility delegate is pending on this source.
- Hosted run 40931055706 passed the complete Android 15 refusal path, including the password-node assertion. Android 11 passed the field check but the synthetic notification reached the TLS ingress and was refused with HTTP 403. The endpoint accepted the same exact source/template in a local synthetic request; the Android journey now records only allowlisted refusal categories so the next hosted run can identify the server-side gate without logging message contents or pairing credentials.
- `uv run pytest -q tests/test_android_journey_diagnostics.py` -> 9 passed; Ruff and `git diff --check` passed. A hosted API 30/35 rerun is required before F4 can advance.
